{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgz978g2P4At3LymMsRgA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still not fixed, and I can see why: none of the changes so far have reached the copy of Natively you're actually running.\n\n- The saved settings file still says `\"isUndetectable\": true`, and it was last modified on May 27. Neither the toggle nor the terminal command changed it.\n- The project folder has no `node_modules` and no build output, so my code change was never built or run.\n- You're running the installed app at `/Applications/Natively.app`, which is a separate build. Editing the project code does nothing to it.\n\nSo the fix is to change the setting the installed app reads, with the app fully closed so it can't save the old value back. My sandbox won't let me write to that folder or quit other apps, so run this in your own terminal:\n\n```sh\nosascript -e 'quit app \"Natively\"'; sleep 2; pkill -x Natively; \\\ncd ~/Library/Application\\ Support/natively && cp settings.json settings.json.bak && \\\nsed -i '' 's/\"isUndetectable\": true/\"isUndetectable\": false/' settings.json && \\\ngrep isUndetectable settings.json && open -a Natively\n```\n\nThat quits Natively, backs up the settings, flips the setting, prints the new value (it should say `false`) and relaunches the app. Then start a Zoom share and the notes should be visible.\n\nIf it prints `false` and the window is still black, tell me. That would mean something else is causing it, and I'd look at Zoom's screen-share settings or macOS screen-recording permissions next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":65104,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagn